  "notes": [
    "Text normalisation: PDF ligature glyphs (ﬁ ﬂ ﬃ ﬀ) rewritten as plain letters; words hyphenated across wrapped table lines re-joined (e.g. 'Pop-pili', 'Madha-varam', 'Kathirve-du', 'NA-GAR'); trailing list commas at the end of single-street cells dropped. Spellings otherwise as printed.",
    "Relief-centre phone numbers on pages 282-284 are printed split over two lines in narrow columns (e.g. '94451' / '90683'); they were joined into 10-digit numbers (9445190683, 9445190323, 9445190083, 9445190324, 9499933621, 9445190326, 9499933625, 9445190331, 9445190325). The joined Sanitary Inspector numbers match officials in the health table.",
    "Relief centres: intro says 5 centres with total capacity 695, but printed capacities sum to 775. Centre 1 is printed as ward 22 (zone 3 is wards 23-33 per the Zonal Officer row, though the ward map title says '22 TO 33'). The relief-shelter map (page 285) disagrees with the table on several wards/names: map R2 = '22 Kannappasamy Nagar 6th St Middle School' (table: ward 24 Poppili Raja Higher Sec. School), map R3 = ward 25 Sembiam Road Middle School (table: ward 31). Table values used. All 5 centres printed Toilets Yes / Drinking water Yes / Cooking Yes.",
    "Relief centre contact roles: Sanitary Inspector = Sanitation, Medicine; Assistant Engineer = Evacuation & Relief Materials; Assistant Revenue Officer = Food & Drinking water.",
    "Inundation table (pages 275-277, 35 rows, NEM 2021) is the heavy-rain list. It has only a 'Capacity of pumps' column (no pump location, depth or days to drain); where that cell describes works rather than a pump (e.g. 'Kutcha Drain Formed', 'Hume Pipe laid'), it is copied into pump as printed.",
    "Inundation row 15 (ward 27, Sakunthala Street): cells interleave; reconstructed as pump cell 'Kutcha drain to Peruyasekkadu Perumal Koil Street' and disposal 'Periyasekkadu Perumal Koil Street' - check against PDF.",
    "Sewer-block stagnation (page 282) is free text, split into 5 ward-26 entries: 'Sewage over flow at Thirumalai Nagar Extn. Thirumalai Nagar, Sastri Nagar, Devaki Nagar, Vajravel Nagar areas due to non availability of pumping station and sewage pipe line leakages In Division 26.' Mild and moderate lists are identical (2 rows each).",
    "Water entered houses (pages 286-288): row 46 is missing in the source (numbering jumps from 45 to 47); 77 rows recorded. Intro mentions 78 / 80 spots. Photo captions disagree with table wards: 'Secretariat Colony, ward 26' (table: ward 30) and 'Pukraj Nagar (Partly), ward -30' (table: ward 25).",
    "Evacuation table (page 289) gives year 2021 although the intro paragraph refers to the 2015 flood; total 50 persons.",
    "Boats (page 293): two rows are printed as ward 21 (Arignar Anna Nagar, Rajiv Gandhi Nagar), outside this zone's wards; kept as printed. Rows 1, 2, 4, 5 give only one location, read as the evacuation area (the page 296 map lists them as evacuation areas E1-E5); stationed location null. Map lists boat stations B1 '22, 24, 25 Division 24, Division Office' and B2 '26, 33 Division 26, Omakulam Madu'. The page 296 map's NDRF ward numbers also differ from the page 292 table (table used).",
    "Lighting (page 292): wards 31 and 32 appear under both Assistant Engineers; ward 25 is under neither. 1 battery powered light in the zone.",
    "Zone 3 has no Chairman row, no subway, no TNSCB tenements, no UPHC/hospital table, and no zonal office address. Veterinary Surgeon 9445026042 is the same number as in zone 2; Senior Entomologist 9445025818 is the same number as a zone 2 relief-centre Sanitary Inspector.",
    "Parks: intro says 41 parks but the table has 63 rows; rows 5 and 8 are identical ('V.S. Mani Nagar 3rd Street Park-4'). name = 'Location of the Park' column, location = 'Name Of Ward' column.",
